  "about": "ND-9a oracle: what each corpus event SHOULD produce, written from the night desk design (sections 2.1, 2.2, 2.7) BEFORE any harness existed or ran. Each event is replayed alone against a fresh store. outcome: posted | refused | accepted | untrusted (the parsers). trust: the event's stored trust. alert: the post asked for an alert (an untrusted event that opened an incident). created: false for a replay of a stored (sensor, seq). text: none | plain (stored as given) | marked (unshowable characters replaced) | capped (cut to the 1000-character bound). refusal: the refused class (EventRefused, or EventConflict for a reused sequence number). why: a part of the door's own message, which must appear in it, so a refusal for the wrong reason disagrees. A key an entry leaves out is not compared; a key it names that the harness did not observe is a disagreement.",
